<Layout>
  <div>
    <h1 class="mb-8 text-center text-3xl font-bold">Pamela Rafalow Grossman</h1>
    <p class="mx-auto max-w-prose">
      Pamela Rafalow Grossman is a nationally published journalist (the <em
        >New York Times</em
      >, Salon.com, <em>Time</em>, etc.) and has edited for many major outlets,
      including <em>Rolling Stone</em> and <em>Real Simple</em> magazines. Her interests,
      professionally and personally, include environmentalism; women&#39;s health
      (with a focus on patient advocacy); poetry; film (especially documentary); and
      music of all kinds. Her Substack, &quot;Communally,&quot; explores how communities
      are created, found, threatened, or preserved. Pamela is in the process of making
      her first short documentary, on the theme of lifelong friendship. She lives
      in Brooklyn, NY, and is an active member of the North Brooklyn Community Boathouse;
      the group leads canoe and kayak trips that launch onto the Newtown Creek, a
      Superfund site, and continue onto the East River.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
